  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has complex roots since D <math><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Complex roots occur in conjugate pair if the coefficients are real.<br />Hence, if it is given that one root of the equations is common, both roots will be common.<br />So, the coefficients of the equations will be proportional<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></math>",
